      "idempotency": "none",
      "status": "defined",
      "evidence": [
        "lumeri_runtime/agent_turn.py:594-652",
        "lumeri_runtime/agent_turn.py:804-830",
        "lumeri_runtime/agent_turn.py:837-970"
      ],
      "notes": "Original Python constructor also receives live app, toolbox, store, optional on_finish and the optional loop (a LoopRun from WorkerApplication._agent_loop); those are Runtime-owned dependencies, not child inputs. No whole-turn deadline or step cap exists; the Session budget bounds paid steps. Re-running run with an active checkpoint for the same root_turn_id resumes from the checkpoint without repeating settled model steps or governed writes."
    },
    {
      "name": "exchange",
      "effect": "process",
      "input": {
        "$contract": "contracts/interfaces/agent/agent.loop.v1.json#/definitions/request"
      },
      "output": {
        "$contract": "contracts/interfaces/agent/agent.loop.v1.json#/definitions/response"
      },
      "errors": [],
      "deadline_ms": 10000,
      "idempotency": "natural",
      "status": "defined",
      "evidence": [
        "lumeri_runtime/luc_agent_loop.py:627-768",
        "lumeri_runtime/luc_agent_loop.py:567-624",
        "lumeri_runtime/luc_sandbox.py:267-339"
      ],
      "notes": "One request line, one answer line. The Runtime sends turn_start (the creator's message and the settled history before it, at most window_messages - 1 messages), then model_reply after each model step, tool_result after each answered call (content is the exact text the conversation keeps), and guidance when the creator spoke before a model step. A model step that the Runtime refuses, that fails, or whose answer is never confirmed ends the turn without asking the program, and none of these is a break. Checks: run_call and skip_call name only the next unanswered call; ask_model only once every call is answered, with a window that equals the newest 1..window_messages messages of the Runtime's conversation and starts at a user message; a completed end only right after a model reply in words with no calls; a failed end only with a reason the program may give. Anything else is a break. 1.1.0 settled the draft envelope at its first implementation: optional history and content fields; an end that completes carries no reason; a failed end's reasons narrowed to the program's own; skip reasons bounded."
    },
    {
      "name": "checkpoint",
      "effect": "write",
      "input": {
        "$contract": "contracts/interfaces/agent/agent.loop.v1.json#/definitions/checkpoint"
      },
      "output": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "persisted": {
            "const": true
          },
          "idempotency_key": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "persisted",
          "idempotency_key"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "errors": [],
      "deadline_ms": null,
      "idempotency": "idempotency_key",
      "status": "defined",
      "evidence": [
        "lumeri_runtime/luc_agent_loop.py:228-256",
        "lumeri_runtime/luc_agent_loop.py:345-564",
        "lumeri_runtime/luc_agent_loop.py:655-658"
      ],
      "notes": "Runtime-only. Before the Runtime performs an action it writes the action, the program's state and the idempotency key (turn_id.m{step} for a model step, turn_id.t{step}.{index} for a call, turn_id.end for an end) with committed false; after the result is in the conversation it writes the result with committed true. One file per Session (agent-loop-checkpoint.json), written aside, renamed and synced, and read back by recover_checkpoint on crash recovery."
    },
    {
      "name": "cancel",
